<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Severan dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">193–235</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Severan dynasty ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> from 193 to 235. It was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus">Septimius Severus</a>, a native of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leptis-magna">Leptis Magna</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, who won the civil wars after 193, and continued under his sons <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caracalla">Caracalla</a> and Geta and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elagabalus">Elagabalus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/severus-alexander">Severus Alexander</a>, relatives of his wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julia-domna">Julia Domna</a>. The murder of Severus Alexander in 235 opened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crisis-of-the-third-century">Crisis of the Third Century</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/severan-dynasty.jpg" alt="Severan dynasty" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_family_of_Septimius_Severus_-_Altes_Museum_-_Berlin_-_Germany_2017.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
